{ genieformats.a68 - the module Genie_Formats of a68j: formatted output in
  the manner of Algol 68 Genie (printf, putf, writef), on top of the module
  Genie_Transput.

  ga68, and a68j with it, has no format texts ($ ... $) and no mode
  format.  The rewrite tool tools/formats/rewrite.a68 turns each format
  text of a program into a call of gfmt or gfmtd, and the mode format
  into Gformat:

      format f = $n(k)(g(0)" "), l$;         becomes
      Gformat f = gfmtd ("n(@1)(g(0)"" ""), l",
                         (int gfindex) int: case gfindex in k esac, skip);

  The string is the format text itself.  A unit of the format text inside
  n(...), g(...) and h(...) that is an integer denotation stays in the
  string; any other unit there and the unit of f(...) is replaced by @ and
  its index.  The procedures after the string yield the unit of an index
  (skip if there is none), so that it is elaborated when the format is
  used, as in Algol 68 Genie.  The rewritten program
  accesses this module besides Genie_Transput:

      access Genie_Transput, Genie_Formats ( ... )

  It is bundled with a68j-backend.jar, and it is written in plain Algol 68
  without Java, so the same source compiles with ga68 as an ordinary
  module.

  What it provides:

      Gformat           the mode of formats
      gfmt, gfmtd       a format from the text of a format text, and the
                        procedures of its dynamic parts
      Gfout             the values putf accepts: those of Outitem of
                        Genie_Transput, and formats
      putf (f, items), printf (items), writef (items)
                        formatted output
      Gfile, Gchannel   other names of File and Channel of Genie_Transput,
                        for programs in UPPER stropping, where FILE and
                        CHANNEL are reserved words of ga68

  The semantics follow Algol 68 Genie:
  - The items are straightened: a row gives its elements, one by one.
  - A value is edited by the next pattern of the format; the insertions
    before and after it are written.  When the format ends and values are
    left, it starts again.  The program ends with the error
      "patterns exhausted in format"
    if a value finds no pattern at all, and with
      "number of pictures does not match number of arguments"
    if patterns of the format are left when its values end.
  - A format item starts a new format; the old one must be used up.
  - Replicators n(...), the parameters of g and the format of f(...) are
    elaborated each time they are reached.
  - g edits a value as print does; g(w) as whole (x, w), g(w, d) as
    fixed (x, w, d) and g(w, d, e) as float (x, w, d, e), for numbers only.
  - Pictures: frames without a comma between them form one picture, with
    the insertions between them; $3d 2d$ takes one value of five digits.
    Integral pictures (d z, a sign + or -) take integers, real pictures
    (with . or e) integers and reals, radix pictures (2r ... 16r) bits,
    and a pictures characters and strings of exactly their length.  z
    writes a blank for a leading zero, and an insertion among such
    blanks is written as blanks; s suppresses a frame.  A sign frame
    after z frames floats to the first digit, as does the sign of a real
    mantissa.  A value that does not fit its picture ends the program
    with "error transputting ... value".
  - b("yes", "no") writes one of its strings for a boolean (b alone T or
    F), c("a", "b", ...) the string of an integer from 1, or nothing.
  - k writes blanks up to the character position of its replicator,
    never backwards.
  - The procedures newline, space ... of Genie_Transput may be items of
    putf (Algol 68 Genie does not allow them); they are called and use no
    pattern.

  Where Algol 68 Genie is defective, this module differs from it
  (docs/genie-formats.md): it keeps the sign of a real whose integral
  digits are all blank, the rest of the line after a number 0 whose
  frames are all z, and counts the position of k from the start of the
  line, not from the start of printf.

  Not provided yet: the complex pattern i, the pattern h, and formatted
  input (getf, readf).  Without i, a complex number is two values, its
  parts, each edited by its own pattern, as in Algol 68 Genie.  A format text that uses i or h is accepted by
  the rewrite tool and ends the program with the error
    "format item ... is not supported yet"
  when the format is elaborated.

  Restrictions, so that tools/formats_tests.py can make an Algol 68 Genie
  version of this module (in UPPER stropping, without the module frame)
  and compare it with the formats of Algol 68 Genie itself: no string
  breaks, only those names of Genie_Transput that Algol 68 Genie has with
  the same meaning (except col of a File in gf_column, which the test
  replaces), and no other module.  Not ]] in SUPPER stropping, where it
  ends a pragmat: a[b[i] ] instead of a[b[i]]. }

module Genie_Formats =
access Genie_Transput
def
    pub mode Gfile = File, Gchannel = Channel;

    { A replicator or a parameter: a constant, or (dyn > 0) the index of a
      dynamic part, the argument of ints of the format. }
    mode Gfrep = struct (int value, dyn);

    { The kinds of the items of a format. }
    int gf_insertion = 1,   { a string, rep times }
        gf_alignment = 2,   { x y l p q, rep times; k: to the position rep }
        gf_general = 3,     { g with its parameters args }
        gf_collection = 4,  { the items sub, rep times }
        gf_format = 5,      { f: the format with the index dyn of rep }
        gf_picture = 6,     { a picture of the class letter: d integral, .
                              real, r radix (the radix is rep), a string;
                              sub are its frames and the insertions
                              between them }
        gf_frame = 7,       { a frame of a picture: letter (d z + - . e a),
                              rep times; text is "s" if it is suppressed }
        gf_choice = 8;      { b or c (letter) with the strings sub }

    mode Gfitem = struct (int kind, char letter, Gfrep rep, string text,
                          ref [] Gfitem sub, ref [] Gfrep args);

    { A format: its items, and the procedures that yield the dynamic
      parts of a given index. }
    pub mode Gformat = struct (ref [] Gfitem items,
                               proc (int) int ints,
                               proc (int) Gformat formats);

    pub mode Gfout = union (int, long int, long long int,
                            real, long real, long long real,
                            compl, long compl, long long compl,
                            bool, char, string, bits, long bits, long long bits,
                            [] int, [] long int, [] real, [] long real,
                            [] bool, [] string, [] bits,
                            [,] int, [,] real, [,] bool,
                            proc (ref File) void,
                            Gformat);

    { A format error ends the program, as in Genie_Transput. }
    proc gf_error = (string message) void:
       begin put (stand_error, ("runtime error: ", message, newline));
             posix_exit (1)
       end;

    proc gf_blank = (char c) bool: c = " " OR c = REPR 10 OR c = REPR 9 OR c = REPR 13;
    proc gf_digit = (char c) bool: c >= "0" AND c <= "9";
    proc gf_lower = (char c) char: (c >= "A" AND c <= "Z" | REPR (ABS c + 32) | c);

    proc gf_member = (char c, string s) bool:
       begin bool found := false;
             for i from LWB s to UPB s do if s[i] = c then found := true fi od;
             found
       end;

    { Parsing.  The text is that of a format text; the units of its
      dynamic parts are replaced by @ and their indices. }

    proc gf_skip_blanks = (string t, ref int pos) void:
       while if pos <= UPB t then gf_blank (t[pos]) else false fi do pos +:= 1 od;

    proc gf_expect = (string t, ref int pos, char c) void:
       begin gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = c else false fi
             then pos +:= 1
             else gf_error ("""" + c + """ expected in format text " + t)
             fi
       end;

    proc gf_number = (string t, ref int pos) int:
       begin gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if if pos <= UPB t then NOT gf_digit (t[pos]) else true fi
             then gf_error ("number expected in format text " + t)
             fi;
             int v := 0;
             while if pos <= UPB t then gf_digit (t[pos]) else false fi
             do v := 10 * v + (ABS t[pos] - ABS "0"); pos +:= 1 od;
             v
       end;

    { The string of a literal insertion starting at pos; a doubled quote
      stands for one quote. }
    proc gf_literal = (string t, ref int pos) string:
       begin string s;
             bool done := false;
             pos +:= 1;
             while NOT done
             do if pos > UPB t
                then gf_error ("unterminated string in format text " + t)
                elif t[pos] /= """"
                then s +:= t[pos]; pos +:= 1
                elif if pos < UPB t then t[pos + 1] = """" else false fi
                then s +:= """"; pos +:= 2
                else pos +:= 1; done := true
                fi
             od;
             s
       end;

    { A parameter or a dynamic replicator: @i, the index of a dynamic
      part, or an integer with an optional sign. }
    proc gf_param = (string t, ref int pos) Gfrep:
       begin gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "@" else false fi
             then pos +:= 1;
                  (0, gf_number (t, pos))
             elif if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "-" else false fi
             then pos +:= 1;
                  (-gf_number (t, pos), 0)
             else if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "+" else false fi then pos +:= 1 fi;
                  (gf_number (t, pos), 0)
             fi
       end;

    { The parameters (p, ...) of g or f. }
    proc gf_args = (string t, ref int pos) ref [] Gfrep:
       begin flex [1 : 0] Gfrep args;
             gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "(" else false fi
             then pos +:= 1;
                  bool more := true;
                  while more
                  do Gfrep p = gf_param (t, pos);
                     [UPB args + 1] Gfrep a;
                     a[: UPB args] := args;
                     a[UPB args + 1] := p;
                     args := a;
                     gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
                     if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "," else false fi
                     then pos +:= 1
                     else more := false
                     fi
                  od;
                  gf_expect (t, pos, ")")
             fi;
             heap [UPB args] Gfrep := args
       end;

    proc gf_append = (ref flex [] Gfitem list, Gfitem it) void:
       begin [UPB list + 1] Gfitem l;
             l[: UPB list] := list;
             l[UPB list + 1] := it;
             list := l
       end;

    { The strings of b(...) and c(...); b may have none. }
    proc gf_choices = (string t, ref int pos, char c) ref [] Gfitem:
       begin flex [1 : 0] Gfitem list;
             gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "(" else false fi
             then pos +:= 1;
                  bool more := true;
                  while more
                  do gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
                     if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] /= """" else true fi
                     then gf_error ("string expected in format text " + t)
                     fi;
                     gf_append (list, (gf_insertion, " ", (1, 0), gf_literal (t, pos),
                                       heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, heap [1 : 0] Gfrep));
                     gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
                     if if pos <= UPB t then t[pos] = "," else false fi
                     then pos +:= 1
                     else more := false
                     fi
                  od;
                  gf_expect (t, pos, ")")
             fi;
             if (c = "b" | UPB list /= 0 AND UPB list /= 2 | UPB list = 0)
             then gf_error ("wrong number of strings of " + c + " in format text " + t)
             fi;
             heap [UPB list] Gfitem := list
       end;

    { An optional replicator: an integer, or n(...). }
    proc gf_replicator = (string t, ref int pos) Gfrep:
       begin gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if pos > UPB t
             then (1, 0)
             elif gf_digit (t[pos])
             then (gf_number (t, pos), 0)
             elif gf_lower (t[pos]) = "n"
             then pos +:= 1;
                  gf_expect (t, pos, "(");
                  Gfrep r = gf_param (t, pos);
                  gf_expect (t, pos, ")");
                  r
             else (1, 0)
             fi
       end;

    { A picture, from its first frame on (or from its radix r): the frames
      and the insertions between them, up to the first item that is not a
      frame of it.  REP is the replicator of the first frame, or the radix.
      Frames without a comma between them make one picture, as in Algol 68
      Genie: $3d 2d$ takes one value of five digits. }
    proc gf_parse_picture = (string t, ref int pos, Gfrep rep, bool radix) Gfitem:
       begin flex [1 : 0] Gfitem list;
             char class := (radix | "r" | " ");
             { The part of a number: 1 the integral part, 2 the fraction,
               3 the exponent; the digit frames of each part; whether the
               current part has a sign frame or a frame d (after which no
               sign may come). }
             int part := 1;
             [3] int digits := (0, 0, 0);
             bool signed := false, has_d := false;
             Gfrep r := rep;
             if radix then pos +:= 1; r := gf_replicator (t, pos) fi;
             bool more := true;
             while more
             do gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
                bool suppressed = if pos <= UPB t then gf_lower (t[pos]) = "s" else false fi;
                if suppressed then pos +:= 1; gf_skip_blanks (t, pos) fi;
                char c = (pos <= UPB t | gf_lower (t[pos]) | " ");
                bool number = class = " " OR class = "d" OR class = ".";
                bool fits =
                   if c = "a" then class = " " OR class = "a"
                   elif c = "d" OR c = "z" then class /= "a"
                   elif c = "+" OR c = "-" then number AND part /= 2 AND NOT signed AND NOT has_d
                   elif c = "." then number AND part = 1
                   elif c = "e" then number AND part < 3
                   else false
                   fi;
                if NOT fits
                then gf_error ("error in format text " + t + " at """ + c + """")
                fi;
                if c = "a" then class := "a"
                elif c = "d" OR c = "z"
                then (class = " " | class := "d");
                     digits[part] +:= 1;
                     (c = "d" | has_d := true)
                elif c = "+" OR c = "-"
                then (class = " " | class := "d");
                     signed := true
                else class := ".";
                     part := (c = "." | 2 | 3);
                     signed := has_d := false
                fi;
                pos +:= 1;
                gf_append (list, (gf_frame, c, r, (suppressed | "s" | ""),
                                  heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, heap [1 : 0] Gfrep));
                { The insertions up to the next frame belong to the picture;
                  if no frame follows, the picture ends after this frame. }
                int after = pos;
                flex [1 : 0] Gfitem insertions;
                bool look := true;
                while look
                do int start = pos;
                   Gfrep nrep = gf_replicator (t, pos);
                   gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
                   char d = (pos <= UPB t | gf_lower (t[pos]) | " ");
                   if gf_member (d, "dzs+-.ea")
                   then r := nrep;
                        for i to UPB insertions do gf_append (list, insertions[i]) od;
                        look := false
                   elif d = """" OR gf_member (d, "xylpqk")
                   then pos := start;
                        gf_append (insertions, gf_parse_item (t, pos))
                   else pos := after;
                        look := more := false
                   fi
                od
             od;
             if (class = "a" | false |: class = "." | digits[1] + digits[2] = 0 OR (part = 3 AND digits[3] = 0)
                 | digits[1] = 0)
             then gf_error ("picture without digit frames in format text " + t)
             fi;
             (gf_picture, class, (radix | rep | (1, 0)), "", heap [UPB list] Gfitem := list,
              heap [1 : 0] Gfrep)
       end;

    proc gf_one = (Gfitem it) ref [] Gfitem:
       begin ref [] Gfitem r = heap [1 : 1] Gfitem;
             r[1] := it;
             r
       end;

    proc gf_parse_item = (string t, ref int pos) Gfitem:
       begin Gfrep rep := (1, 0);
             bool replicated := false;
             char c0 = t[pos];
             if gf_digit (c0)
             then rep := (gf_number (t, pos), 0); replicated := true
             elif gf_lower (c0) = "n"
             then pos +:= 1;
                  gf_expect (t, pos, "(");
                  rep := gf_param (t, pos);
                  gf_expect (t, pos, ")");
                  replicated := true
             fi;
             gf_skip_blanks (t, pos);
             if pos > UPB t then gf_error ("replicator without an item in format text " + t) fi;
             char c = gf_lower (t[pos]);
             { A pattern with a replicator is a collection of that pattern. }
             proc replicate = (Gfitem it) Gfitem:
                (replicated | (gf_collection, " ", rep, "", gf_one (it), heap [1 : 0] Gfrep) | it);
             if c = "("
             then pos +:= 1;
                  (gf_collection, " ", rep, "", gf_parse_list (t, pos, true), heap [1 : 0] Gfrep)
             elif c = """"
             then (gf_insertion, " ", rep, gf_literal (t, pos), heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, heap [1 : 0] Gfrep)
             elif gf_member (c, "xylpqk")
             then pos +:= 1;
                  (gf_alignment, c, rep, "", heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, heap [1 : 0] Gfrep)
             elif c = "g"
             then pos +:= 1;
                  ref [] Gfrep args = gf_args (t, pos);
                  if UPB args > 3 then gf_error ("too many parameters of g in format text " + t) fi;
                  replicate ((gf_general, c, (1, 0), "", heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, args))
             elif c = "f"
             then pos +:= 1;
                  ref [] Gfrep args = gf_args (t, pos);
                  if UPB args /= 1 then gf_error ("f needs one format in format text " + t)
                  elif dyn of args[1] = 0 then gf_error ("f needs a format in format text " + t)
                  fi;
                  replicate ((gf_format, c, args[1], "", heap [1 : 0] Gfitem, heap [1 : 0] Gfrep))
             elif gf_member (c, "dzs+-.ea")
             then gf_parse_picture (t, pos, rep, false)
             elif c = "r"
             then if NOT replicated OR dyn of rep /= 0 OR value of rep < 2 OR value of rep > 16
                  then gf_error ("radix from 2 to 16 expected in format text " + t)
                  fi;
                  gf_parse_picture (t, pos, rep, true)
             elif c = "b" OR c = "c"
             then pos +:= 1;
                  replicate ((gf_choice, c, (1, 0), "", gf_choices (t, pos, c), heap [1 : 0] Gfrep))
             elif gf_member (c, "ih")
             then gf_error ("format item " + c + " is not supported yet (format text " + t + ")"); skip
             else gf_error ("error in format text " + t + " at """ + c + """"); skip
             fi
       end;

    { The items up to the end of the text, or (nested) up to the closing
      parenthesis of a collection. }
    proc gf_parse_list = (string t, ref int pos, bool nested) ref [] Gfitem:
       begin flex [1 : 0] Gfitem list;
             bool done := false;
             while NOT done
             do while if pos <= UPB t then gf_blank (t[pos]) OR t[pos] = "," else false fi
                do pos +:= 1 od;
                if pos > UPB t
                then if nested then gf_error ("missing "")"" in format text " + t) fi;
                     done := true
                elif t[pos] = ")"
                then if NOT nested then gf_error ("unexpected "")"" in format text " + t) fi;
                     pos +:= 1;
                     done := true
                else Gfitem it = gf_parse_item (t, pos);
                     [UPB list + 1] Gfitem l;
                     l[: UPB list] := list;
                     l[UPB list + 1] := it;
                     list := l
                fi
             od;
             heap [UPB list] Gfitem := list
       end;

    { The parsed format texts, in a small cache, so that a format text in
      a loop is parsed once.  The items have no procedures, so they may
      live in the heap.  Each entry is one name, so that a parallel clause
      never sees half an entry. }
    mode Gfparsed = struct (string text, ref [] Gfitem items);
    int gf_cache_size = 64;
    ref [] ref Gfparsed gf_cache = heap [0 : gf_cache_size - 1] ref Gfparsed;
    for i from 0 to gf_cache_size - 1 do gf_cache[i] := nil od;

    proc gf_parsed = (string text) ref [] Gfitem:
       begin int h := 0;
             for i from LWB text to UPB text do h := (31 * h + ABS text[i]) MOD gf_cache_size od;
             ref Gfparsed e = gf_cache[h];
             if if e isnt nil then text of e = text else false fi
             then items of e
             else int pos := LWB text;
                  ref [] Gfitem items = gf_parse_list (text, pos, false);
                  gf_cache[h] := heap Gfparsed := (text, items);
                  items
             fi
       end;

    pub proc gfmtd = (string text, proc (int) int ints, proc (int) Gformat formats) Gformat:
       Gformat (gf_parsed (text), ints, formats);

    proc gf_no_ints = (int i) int: (gf_error ("no dynamic part @" + whole (i, 0) + " in format"); 0);
    proc gf_no_formats = (int i) Gformat: (gf_error ("no format @" + whole (i, 0) + " in format"); skip);

    pub proc gfmt = (string text) Gformat: gfmtd (text, gf_no_ints, gf_no_formats);

    { Output. }

    proc gf_rep = (Gfrep r, Gformat ctx) int:
       if dyn of r = 0 then value of r
       else (ints of ctx) (dyn of r)
       fi;

    proc gf_mode_name = (Gfout v) string:
       case v
       in (int x): "INT",
          (long int x): "LONG INT",
          (long long int x): "LONG LONG INT",
          (real x): "REAL",
          (long real x): "LONG REAL",
          (long long real x): "LONG LONG REAL",
          (bool x): "BOOL",
          (char x): "CHAR",
          (string x): "[] CHAR",
          (bits x): "BITS",
          (long bits x): "LONG BITS",
          (long long bits x): "LONG LONG BITS"
       out "this"
       esac;

    { The value V does not fit a pattern of the kind PATTERN. }
    proc gf_cannot = (Gfout v, string pattern) void:
       gf_error ("cannot transput " + gf_mode_name (v) + " value with " + pattern + "-pattern");

    { The alignment k: blanks up to the character position c of the line,
      never backwards. }
    proc gf_column = (ref File f, int c) void: while col of f + 1 < c do space (f) od;

    { The alignment C (x y l p q), N times; k moves to the position N. }
    proc gf_align = (ref File f, char c, int n) void:
       if c = "k"
       then gf_column (f, n)
       else to n
            do if c = "x" OR c = "q" then space (f)
               elif c = "y" then backspace (f)
               elif c = "l" then newline (f)
               elif c = "p" then newpage (f)
               fi
            od
       fi;

    { The value V edited by the general pattern IT. }
    proc gf_general_out = (ref File f, Gfitem it, Gformat ctx, Gfout v) void:
       begin int n = UPB args of it;
             [n] int a;
             for i to n do a[i] := gf_rep ((args of it)[i], ctx) od;
             case v
             in (int x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (long int x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (long long int x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (real x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (long real x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (long long real x):
                   (n = 0 | put (f, x) |: n = 1 | put (f, whole (x, a[1]))
                    |: n = 2 | put (f, fixed (x, a[1], a[2])) | put (f, float (x, a[1], a[2], a[3]))),
                (bool x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general")),
                (char x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general")),
                (string x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general")),
                (bits x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general")),
                (long bits x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general")),
                (long long bits x): (n = 0 | put (f, x) | gf_cannot (v, "general"))
             out gf_cannot (v, "general")
             esac
       end;

    { Scales Y to BEFORE integral digits, rounded to AFTER digits, and adds
      the exponent to P: the procedure long_standardize of the standard
      prelude, which is not public. }
    proc gf_standardize = (ref long real y, int before, after, ref int p) void:
       begin long real g = long 10.0 ** before;
             long real h = g * long .1;
             if y /= long 0.0
             then long real x = y;
                  int q := SHORTEN ENTIER long_log (x) - before + 1;
                  proc scale = void:
                     y := (q > 300 | x / long 10.0 ** 300 / long 10.0 ** (q - 300)
                          |: q >= 0 | x / long 10.0 ** q
                          |: q >= -300 | x * long 10.0 ** -q
                          | x * long 10.0 ** 300 * long 10.0 ** (-q - 300));
                  scale;
                  while y >= g do q +:= 1; scale od;
                  while y < h do q -:= 1; scale od;
                  p +:= q
             fi;
             (y + long .5 * long .1 ** after >= g | y := h; p +:= 1)
       end;

    { The digits of an integer, without a sign and without leading zeros
      (none for 0). }
    proc gf_strip = (string s) string:
       begin int i := LWB s;
             while if i <= UPB s then s[i] = "-" OR s[i] = "+" OR s[i] = "0" OR s[i] = " " else false fi
             do i +:= 1 od;
             s[i : ]
       end;

    { The digits of the bits V in the radix R.  The bits are taken with
      SHR: in Algol 68 Genie, ELEM of a long bits value does not yield its
      bits in order. }
    proc gf_radix_digits = (Gfout v, int r) string:
       begin [1 : long_long_bits_width + 1] int d;  { the digits, the lowest first }
             int nd := 0;
             proc add = (bool bit) void:
                begin int carry := (bit | 1 | 0);
                      for i to nd
                      do int x = d[i] * 2 + carry;
                         d[i] := x MOD r;
                         carry := x % r
                      od;
                      while carry > 0 do nd +:= 1; d[nd] := carry MOD r; carry := carry % r od
                end;
             case v
             in (bits b):
                   for i from bits_width - 1 by -1 to 0
                   do add (((b SHR i) AND 16r1) /= 16r0) od,
                (long bits b):
                   for i from long_bits_width - 1 by -1 to 0
                   do add (((b SHR i) AND long 16r1) /= long 16r0) od,
                (long long bits b):
                   for i from long_long_bits_width - 1 by -1 to 0
                   do add (((b SHR i) AND long long 16r1) /= long long 16r0) od
             esac;
             string s;
             string hex = "0123456789abcdef";
             for i from nd by -1 to 1 do s +:= hex[d[i] + 1] od;
             s
       end;

    { Edits the digits D of an integral mould: the elements LO to HI of a
      picture, which are digit frames d and z, at most one sign frame, and
      insertions.  OUTS gets what each frame writes, BLANK whether an
      insertion is written as blanks (in the area of suppressed zeros).
      The sign is written before the frame after the sign frame or, if
      the mould floats (z frames before the sign frame, or the mantissa
      of a real), before the first digit written.  Yields the sign if it
      is still to be written. }
    proc gf_mould = (ref [] int ek, ref [] char el, ref [] string outs, ref [] bool blank, int lo, hi,
                     string d, bool negative, floating_mantissa, string name) string:
       begin int nd := 0, sign_at := 0;
             bool z_before_sign := false;
             for i from lo to hi
             do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                then if el[i] = "d" OR el[i] = "z"
                     then nd +:= 1
                     else sign_at := i; z_before_sign := nd > 0
                     fi
                fi
             od;
             int nd_value = UPB d - LWB d + 1;
             if nd_value > nd then gf_error ("error transputting " + name + " value") fi;
             if negative AND sign_at = 0
             then gf_error ("error transputting sign in " + name + " value")
             fi;
             string digits = (nd - nd_value) * "0" + d;
             string sign = (sign_at = 0 | "" |: negative | "-" |: el[sign_at] = "+" | "+" | " ");
             bool floating = floating_mantissa OR z_before_sign;
             bool sign_todo := sign_at /= 0, sign_passed := false;
             bool suppressing := true, blanked := false;
             int k := 0;
             for i from lo to hi
             do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                then char c = el[i];
                     if c = "d" OR c = "z"
                     then k +:= 1;
                          if c = "z" AND suppressing AND digits[k] = "0"
                          then outs[i] := " "; blanked := true
                          else suppressing := false; outs[i] := digits[k : k]
                          fi;
                          if sign_todo AND (floating | outs[i] /= " " | sign_passed)
                          then outs[i] := sign + outs[i]; sign_todo := false
                          fi
                     else sign_passed := true
                     fi
                elif ek[i] = gf_insertion
                then blank[i] := suppressing AND blanked
                fi
             od;
             (sign_todo | sign | "")
       end;

    { The value V edited by the picture IT. }
    proc gf_picture_out = (ref File f, Gfitem it, Gformat ctx, Gfout v) void:
       begin ref [] Gfitem sub = sub of it;
             { The replicators, each elaborated once. }
             [UPB sub] int reps;
             int n := 0;
             for i to UPB sub
             do reps[i] := gf_rep (rep of sub[i], ctx);
                (reps[i] < 0 | reps[i] := 0);
                n +:= (kind of sub[i] = gf_frame | reps[i] | 1)
             od;
             { The elements: one per frame, one per insertion with its count. }
             [n] int ek, src, count;
             [n] char el;
             [n] bool hidden;
             int m := 0;
             for i to UPB sub
             do if kind of sub[i] = gf_frame
                then to reps[i]
                     do m +:= 1; ek[m] := gf_frame; el[m] := letter of sub[i];
                        hidden[m] := text of sub[i] = "s"; src[m] := i; count[m] := 1
                     od
                else m +:= 1; ek[m] := kind of sub[i]; el[m] := letter of sub[i];
                     hidden[m] := false; src[m] := i; count[m] := reps[i]
                fi
             od;
             [n] string outs;
             [n] bool blank;
             for i to n do outs[i] := ""; blank[i] := false od;
             string name = gf_mode_name (v);
             char class = letter of it;
             if class = "a"
             then int na := 0;
                  for i to n do (ek[i] = gf_frame | na +:= 1) od;
                  string s = case v
                             in (char c):
                                   (na /= 1 | gf_error ("error transputting CHAR value"); "" | "" + c),
                                (string x):
                                   (UPB x - LWB x + 1 /= na | gf_error ("error transputting [] CHAR value"); "" | x)
                             out gf_cannot (v, "string"); ""
                             esac;
                  int k := LWB s - 1;
                  for i to n
                  do if ek[i] = gf_frame then k +:= 1; outs[i] := s[k : k] fi
                  od
             elif class = "r"
             then case v
                  in (bits x): skip,
                     (long bits x): skip,
                     (long long bits x): skip
                  out gf_cannot (v, "bits")
                  esac;
                  string d = gf_strip (gf_radix_digits (v, value of rep of it));
                  string sign = gf_mould (ek, el, outs, blank, 1, n, d, false, false, name);
                  skip
             elif class = "d"
             then string w = case v
                             in (int x): whole (x, 0),
                                (long int x): whole (x, 0),
                                (long long int x): whole (x, 0)
                             out gf_cannot (v, "integral"); ""
                             esac;
                  bool negative = if UPB w >= LWB w then w[LWB w] = "-" else false fi;
                  string sign := gf_mould (ek, el, outs, blank, 1, n, gf_strip (w), negative, false, name);
                  for i from n by -1 to 1
                  do if ek[i] = gf_frame AND sign /= "" then outs[i] +:= sign; sign := "" fi
                  od
             else { A real picture: the integral part, the point, the fraction,
                    and the exponent. }
                  long real y = case v
                                in (int x): LENG real (x),
                                   (long int x): long real (x),
                                   (long long int x): long real (SHORTEN x),
                                   (real x): LENG x,
                                   (long real x): x,
                                   (long long real x): SHORTEN x
                                out gf_cannot (v, "real"); long 0.0
                                esac;
                  int point := 0, ex := 0;
                  for i to n
                  do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                     then (el[i] = "." | point := i |: el[i] = "e" | ex := i)
                     fi
                  od;
                  int int_hi = (point /= 0 | point - 1 |: ex /= 0 | ex - 1 | n);
                  int frac_lo = (point /= 0 | point + 1 | int_hi + 1);
                  int frac_hi = (ex /= 0 | ex - 1 | n);
                  proc digit_frames = (int lo, hi) int:
                     begin int c := 0;
                           for i from lo to hi
                           do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                              then (el[i] = "d" OR el[i] = "z" | c +:= 1)
                              fi
                           od;
                           c
                     end;
                  int before = digit_frames (1, int_hi), after = digit_frames (frac_lo, frac_hi);
                  long real a := ABS y;
                  int p := 0;
                  if ex /= 0 then gf_standardize (a, before, after, p) fi;
                  string s = fixed (a, 0, after);
                  int dot := UPB s + 1;
                  for i from LWB s to UPB s do (s[i] = "." | dot := i) od;
                  string sign := gf_mould (ek, el, outs, blank, 1, int_hi, gf_strip (s[: dot - 1]),
                                           y < long 0.0, true, name);
                  int k := dot;
                  for i from frac_lo to frac_hi
                  do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                     then k +:= 1;
                          outs[i] := (k <= UPB s | s[k : k] | "0")
                     fi
                  od;
                  if point /= 0 then outs[point] := sign + "."; sign := "" fi;
                  if ex /= 0
                  then outs[ex] := sign + "e";
                       string esign = gf_mould (ek, el, outs, blank, ex + 1, n, gf_strip (whole (p, 0)),
                                                p < 0, false, name);
                       skip
                  fi
             fi;
             { Writing, in one piece up to each alignment. }
             string w := "";
             for i to n
             do if ek[i] = gf_frame
                then (NOT hidden[i] | w +:= outs[i])
                elif ek[i] = gf_insertion
                then string s = text of sub[src[i] ];  { not ]]: in SUPPER stropping ]] ends a pragmat }
                     to count[i] do w +:= (blank[i] | (UPB s - LWB s + 1) * " " | s) od
                else put (f, w);
                     w := "";
                     gf_align (f, el[i], count[i])
                fi
             od;
             put (f, w)
       end;

    { The value V edited by the choice pattern IT (b or c). }
    proc gf_choice_out = (ref File f, Gfitem it, Gfout v) void:
       begin ref [] Gfitem s = sub of it;
             if letter of it = "b"
             then case v
                  in (bool x):
                        if UPB s = 0 then put (f, (x | "T" | "F"))
                        else put (f, text of s[(x | 1 | 2)])
                        fi
                  out gf_cannot (v, "boolean")
                  esac
             else case v
                  in (int x): (x >= 1 AND x <= UPB s | put (f, text of s[x]))
                  out gf_cannot (v, "choice")
                  esac
             fi
       end;

    { The state of a format being used: the collections and formats it is
      in.  The current item is items[index] of the last frame; reps is
      the number of times the items of the frame are still to be used. }
    mode Gfframe = struct (ref [] Gfitem items, int index, reps, Gformat ctx);

    pub proc putf = (ref File f, [] Gfout items) void:
       begin { The frames are stack[1 : depth]. }
             { A local row, not the heap: the frames hold the procedures
               of the formats, whose scope is that of their format texts
               (Algol 68 Genie checks it). }
             [1 : 8] Gfframe stack;
             int depth := 0;
             Gformat current;
             bool have_format := false;

             proc push = (ref [] Gfitem its, int reps, Gformat ctx) void:
                begin if depth = UPB stack
                      then gf_error ("formats and collections nested too deeply")
                      fi;
                      depth +:= 1;
                      stack[depth] := (its, 1, reps, ctx)
                end;

             proc pop = void: depth -:= 1;

             proc next = void:
                if depth > 0 then index of stack[depth] +:= 1 fi;

             { Writes the insertions up to the next pattern; true if there
               is one (it is then the current item), false at the end of
               the format. }
             proc seek = bool:
                begin bool found := false, finished := false;
                      while NOT found AND NOT finished
                      do if depth = 0
                         then finished := true
                         elif index of stack[depth] > UPB items of stack[depth]
                         then if reps of stack[depth] > 1
                              then reps of stack[depth] -:= 1;
                                   index of stack[depth] := 1
                              else pop; next
                              fi
                         else Gfframe top = stack[depth];
                              Gfitem it = (items of top)[index of top];
                              int kind = kind of it;
                              if kind = gf_insertion
                              then to gf_rep (rep of it, ctx of top) do put (f, text of it) od;
                                   next
                              elif kind = gf_alignment
                              then gf_align (f, letter of it, gf_rep (rep of it, ctx of top));
                                   next
                              elif kind = gf_collection
                              then int r = gf_rep (rep of it, ctx of top);
                                   if r > 0 then push (sub of it, r, ctx of top) else next fi
                              elif kind = gf_format
                              then Gformat g = (formats of ctx of top) (dyn of rep of it);
                                   push (items of g, 1, g)
                              else found := true
                              fi
                         fi
                      od;
                      found
                end;

             { The current format must be used up. }
             proc finish = void:
                if have_format
                then if seek then gf_error ("number of pictures does not match number of arguments") fi
                fi;

             proc start = (Gformat g) void:
                begin finish;
                      current := g;
                      have_format := true;
                      depth := 0;
                      push (items of g, 1, g)
                end;

             proc out_value = (Gfout v) void:
                begin bool found := if have_format then seek else false fi;
                      if NOT found AND have_format
                      then push (items of current, 1, current);
                           found := seek
                      fi;
                      if NOT found then gf_error ("patterns exhausted in format") fi;
                      Gfframe top = stack[depth];
                      Gfitem it = (items of top)[index of top];
                      next;
                      if kind of it = gf_general then gf_general_out (f, it, ctx of top, v)
                      elif kind of it = gf_picture then gf_picture_out (f, it, ctx of top, v)
                      else gf_choice_out (f, it, v)
                      fi;
                      seek
                end;

             for k from LWB items to UPB items
             do case items[k]
                in (Gformat g): start (g),
                   (proc (ref File) void p): p (f),
                   ([] int r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] long int r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] real r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] long real r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] bool r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] string r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   ([] bits r): for i from LWB r to UPB r do out_value (r[i]) od,
                   { A complex number is two values, as in Algol 68 Genie
                     without the pattern i. }
                   (compl z): (out_value (re of z); out_value (im of z)),
                   (long compl z): (out_value (re of z); out_value (im of z)),
                   (long long compl z): (out_value (re of z); out_value (im of z)),
                   ([,] int r):
                      for i from 1 LWB r to 1 UPB r
                      do for j from 2 LWB r to 2 UPB r do out_value (r[i, j]) od od,
                   ([,] real r):
                      for i from 1 LWB r to 1 UPB r
                      do for j from 2 LWB r to 2 UPB r do out_value (r[i, j]) od od,
                   ([,] bool r):
                      for i from 1 LWB r to 1 UPB r
                      do for j from 2 LWB r to 2 UPB r do out_value (r[i, j]) od od
                out out_value (items[k])
                esac
             od;
             finish
       end;

    pub proc printf = ([] Gfout items) void: putf (stand_out, items);
    pub proc writef = ([] Gfout items) void: putf (stand_out, items);

    skip
fed
